{"name":"Bryophyte","hex":"#a6bea6","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"bryophyte","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any plant of the division Bryophyta, defined sensu lato to comprise the mosses, liverworts and hornworts and corresponding to all embryophytes that are not vascular plants."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bryophyte"}],"entries":[{"title":"Bryophyte","blocks":[{"text":"Bryophytes are a group of land plants (embryophytes), sometimes treated as a taxonomic division referred to as Bryophyta sensu lato, that contains three groups of non-vascular land plants: the liverworts, hornworts, and mosses. In the strict sense, the division Bryophyta consists of the mosses only. Bryophytes are characteristically limited in size and prefer moist habitats although some species can survive in drier environments. The bryophytes consist of about 20,000 plant species. Bryophytes produce enclosed reproductive structures, but they do not produce flowers or seeds. They reproduce sexually by spores and asexually by fragmentation or the production of gemmae."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/11/MarchantiophytaSp.NonD%C3%A9termin%C3%A9eFL3.jpg/330px-MarchantiophytaSp.NonD%C3%A9termin%C3%A9eFL3.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bryophyte","wikidata":"Q29993"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/38/Moss_%28Bryophyta%29_on_the_forest_floor_in_Broken_Bow%2C_Oklahoma.jpg/500px-Moss_%28Bryophyta%29_on_the_forest_floor_in_Broken_Bow%2C_Oklahoma.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/38/Moss_%28Bryophyta%29_on_the_forest_floor_in_Broken_Bow%2C_Oklahoma.jpg/1280px-Moss_%28Bryophyta%29_on_the_forest_floor_in_Broken_Bow%2C_Oklahoma.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnai